note as N_Layers
    **Layers** (v3: v2 + remove and clear, call table and filters, D15 and D16)
    * **ZAP adapter** (input): turns ZAP's events into our input format ""ApiCall"".
      The only layer that knows ZAP's message API.
    * **Presentation** (output): panel and writer. They talk only to the controller
      and read only the report values.
    * **Domain**: ""RestExtractor"" is the controller at its border. Inside, objects
      talk to each other directly. Input ""ApiCall"", output ""ApiReport"".
    * Endpoint templates are relative to their namespace (""/posts/[POST_ID]/comments""):
      origin and base path are checked once, in ""ApiNamespace"".
end note

' ============================================================ ZAP adapter
package "ZAP adapter layer (input), org.zaproxy.addon.restextraction" as adapter {
    class ExtensionRestExtraction {
        + hook(extensionHook: ExtensionHook): void
        + getUIName(): String
        + getDescription(): String
        + canUnload(): boolean
    }
    class RestTrafficListener {
        + RestTrafficListener(extractor: RestExtractor)
        + onHttpRequestSend(msg: HttpMessage): boolean
        + onHttpResponseReceive(msg: HttpMessage): boolean
        + getArrangeableListenerOrder(): int
        - toApiCall(msg: HttpMessage): ApiCall
    }
}

note as N_RestTrafficListener
    **RestTrafficListener** (Adapter, Indirection)

    ""onHttpResponseReceive(msg):""
    ""  extractor.record(toApiCall(msg))""
    ""  return true  // never block traffic""
    ""onHttpRequestSend(msg): return true""

    ""toApiCall"" reads method, URL without query, status code,
    response headers and body from ""msg""; a method not in
    the enum becomes ""OTHER"". A body above 64 KB is cut and a
    binary body is replaced by a mark.
end note

